Why is ApexaiQ an Agentless Platform?
Ans: ApexaiQ is an agentless platform because it eliminates the need to install software agents on individual devices, simplifying deployment and reducing operational disruptions.


Key Concepts
ApexaiQ Score
A numerical score (60-160) that rates the health and security of an IT environment, inspired by human IQ. A higher score indicates better IT hygiene, fewer vulnerabilities, and stronger security.

IT Asset Management (ITAM)
The process of tracking and managing IT assets (hardware, software, etc.) throughout their lifecycle.

Vulnerabilities
Weaknesses in IT systems that could be exploited by cyber threats. ApexaiQ identifies vulnerabilities in devices and software to prioritize remediation.

Obsolescence
Refers to outdated hardware or software that can lead to non-compliance or security risks. ApexaiQ flags end-of-life (EOL) assets for timely replacement.

Maintenance
Regular updates and fixes for IT assets.

End of Life (EOL), End of Support (EOS), End of Maintenance (EOM)

EOL: When an asset is no longer supported by the manufacturer.
EOS/EOM: When updates or support cease. ApexaiQ provides real-time reporting on these statuses for proactive management.
Asset Hygiene
The overall health and security status of IT assets. ApexaiQ does this using its scoring system.

Crown Jewel
Securing the most essential asset best for business operation.

Inventory
Comprehensive tracking of all IT assets (on-premises, cloud, co-located). ApexaiQ automates this.

NVD (National Vulnerability Database)
A U.S. government repository of known vulnerabilities and ways to overcome them.

Patch Management
The process of applying updates to fix vulnerabilities or improve functionality. ApexaiQ prioritizes this based on risk levels.

Data Breaches
Unauthorized access to sensitive data. Data leak.

MSP (Managed Service Provider)
Companies that manage IT services for clients. For us, ApexaiQ.

Device Types
Includes hardware (servers, laptops) and virtual/cloud-based devices.

True SaaS
A fully cloud-based solution accessible anytime without on-premises installation. ApexaiQ is also agentless.

Inbound/Outbound Integration
Connecting with external tools for data exchange. Taking data from various data sources.

Compliance Standards (e.g., CISA, HIPAA, ISO 27001)
Regulatory frameworks ensuring data security and privacy. ApexaiQ automates this.

Perimeter
The boundary between an organization's internal network and external threats. ApexaiQ monitors this.

ROI (Return on Investment), KPI (Key Performance Indicators)

ROI: Measures financial benefits from investments like ITAM tools.
KPI: Metrics to track performance. ApexaiQ provides reports for both.
Auto-remediation
Automated resolution of issues like patching vulnerabilities or updating configurations. ApexaiQ does this with SOAR tools.

Network Protocols
Rules governing communication between devices in a network. Examples: TCP, IP, HTTP, SMTP, FTP, DNS, DHCP, etc.

Due Diligence
The process of assessing risks during mergers or acquisitions.

SOAR (Security Orchestration, Automation, and Response)
Tools that automate threat detection and response workflow. ApexaiQ integrates with SOAR.

Role of ITAM in Zero Trust Security Models
ITAM ensures visibility into all assets, a foundational requirement for Zero Trust models where no device is inherently trusted without verification.

Cyber Asset Attack Surface Management (CAASM)
Identifies all cyber assets to reduce attack surfaces. ApexaiQ combines CAASM with ITAM.
